                <pb facs="0490" n="346" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg346"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77 Chinese Eastern/459: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-22T18:00:00+08:00">November 22, 1929—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 22—11:15 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1026. My 1020, November 21, noon. Following from American Consul at Mukden:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“November 21, 6 p.m. It has been learned from official source today that
                            Manchuli and Chalainor have both been captured by the Soviets. General
                            Han and another general, name unknown, were captured; latter committed
                            suicide.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
